---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---
<BaseLayout title="About VPSTier.com | Independent VPS Reviews & Comparisons" description="VPSTier.com provides independent VPS hosting reviews, comparisons, and buying guides for developers, indie SaaS founders, and AI agent builders.">
  <section class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-6 py-16">
    <a href="/" class="text-orange-500 hover:text-orange-400 text-sm mb-6 block">← Back to Home</a>
    <h1 class="text-4xl font-bold text-white mb-4">About VPSTier.com</h1>
    <p class="text-gray-400 text-sm mb-8">Last updated: June 6, 2026</p>

    <div class="prose prose-invert max-w-none text-gray-300 leading-relaxed space-y-6">
      <p>VPSTier.com is an independent VPS hosting review site. We test and compare VPS providers with a focus on what actually matters to developers, indie SaaS founders, and AI agent builders: real latency, real pricing, real performance — not marketing claims.</p>

      <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-white mt-8 mb-4">What we do</h2>
      <ul class="list-disc pl-6 space-y-2">
        <li><strong>Provider reviews</strong> — Hands-on testing of VPS providers (RackNerd, Vultr, DigitalOcean, Hostinger, ScalaHosting, Contabo, Interserver, Cloudways, UpCloud, and more).</li>
        <li><strong>Buying guides</strong> — Practical guides for choosing a VPS by use case: AI agent hosting, indie SaaS, blog hosting, dev environments, multi-region backup.</li>
        <li><strong>Comparison articles</strong> — Side-by-side comparisons of providers, regions, and pricing tiers.</li>
        <li><strong>Vendor risk analysis</strong> — Coverage of provider shutdowns, account issues, and infrastructure failures that affect self-hosters.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-white mt-8 mb-4">How we test</h2>
      <p>Each provider review is based on real deployments. We measure:</p>
      <ul class="list-disc pl-6 space-y-2">
        <li>Real-world latency from multiple source IPs to provider data centers</li>
        <li>Hourly billing flexibility (or lack thereof)</li>
        <li>Support response time and quality</li>
        <li>Resource limits and throttling behavior on cheap plans</li>
        <li>Network performance for AI inference and database workloads</li>
      </ul>

      <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-white mt-8 mb-4">How we make money</h2>
      <p>VPSTier.com participates in affiliate programs with several VPS providers. When you click a provider link in our reviews and sign up, we may earn a small commission at no extra cost to you. This is how the site stays independent — we don't take paid placements or sponsored reviews.</p>
      <p>Our editorial recommendations are not influenced by affiliate relationships. If a provider pays us nothing, we still recommend them if they're the best fit for the use case (and vice versa).</p>

      <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-white mt-8 mb-4">Who runs VPSTier.com</h2>
      <p>VPSTier.com is run by Jason Mai, a developer and infrastructure tinkerer. Read more on <a href="https://about.me/jasonxmai" rel="me noopener" target="_blank" class="text-orange-500 hover:text-orange-400">About.me</a> or check out our sister projects: <a href="https://apirank.vip" rel="noopener" target="_blank" class="text-orange-500 hover:text-orange-400">APIRank</a> (AI API reviews) and <a href="https://md2rich.com" rel="noopener" target="_blank" class="text-orange-500 hover:text-orange-400">md2rich</a> (Markdown tools).</p>

      <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-white mt-8 mb-4">Contact</h2>
      <p>For corrections, suggestions, or partnership inquiries, reach out via the About.me profile linked above.</p>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
